In Kafka-streams 3.4.0 :

According to the javadoc of the Joinwindow:

_There are three different window configuration supported:_
 * _before =3D after =3D time-difference_
 * _before =3D 0 and after =3D time-difference_
 * _*before =3D time-difference and after =3D 0*_

=C2=A0

However if=C2=A0I use a joinWindow with *before =3D time-difference and aft=
er =3D 0*=20
on a kstream-kstream-leftjoin the *after=3D0* part does not seem to work.

When using _stream1.leftjoin(stream2, joinWindow)_ with {_}joinWindow{_}.{_=
}after=3D0 and joinWindow.before=3D30s{_}, any new message on stream 1 that=
 can not be joined with any messages on stream2 should be joined with a nul=
l-record after the _joinWindow.after_ has ended and a new message has arriv=
ed on stream1.

It does not.

Only if the new message arrives after the value of _joinWindow.before_ the =
previous message will be joined with a null-record.

=C2=A0

Attached you can find two files with a TopologyTestDriver Unit test to repr=
oduce.

topology:=C2=A0 =C2=A0stream1.leftjoin( stream2, joiner, joinwindow)

joinWindow has before=3D5000ms and after=3D0

message1(key1) ->=C2=A0 stream1

after 4000ms message2(key2) -> stream1=C2=A0 ->=C2=A0 NO null-record join w=
as made, but the after period was expired.
after 4900ms message2(key2) -> stream1=C2=A0 ->=C2=A0 NO null-record join w=
as made, but the after period was expired.
after 5000ms message2(key2) -> stream1=C2=A0 ->=C2=A0 A null-record join wa=
s made,=C2=A0 before period was expired.
after 6000ms message2(key2) -> stream1=C2=A0 ->=C2=A0 A null-record join wa=
s made,=C2=A0 before period was expired.



